## What to do

Visit the URL above and read what it actually says — do not rely on a title
or a guess at its contents. Then compare the marked code against it.

## Pass

The marked code implements the same contract the doc describes at that URL —
same trajectory-JSONL shape, same hook names and firing conditions, same
field names — under the doc's CURRENT wording (fetched live), not an earlier
or assumed version of it.

## Fail

- The URL does not resolve, or its content has nothing to do with what the
  marker claims — refuse and say so; there is nothing to verify conformance
  against.
- The mock emits or expects a shape the doc does not describe (a field the
  real implementation dropped, a hook the real one never fires).
- The mock implements what the doc used to say rather than what it currently
  says — the code has not caught up to a doc change.
- The marker sits on code unrelated to what the doc is actually describing —
  a marker placed hopefully rather than accurately.

Name the specific line and quote the exact clause of the doc (as fetched)
that it fails to match.
